      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022paragraphs\u0022:[[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The bull case rests on revenue of $1.85 billion for the quarter ended 2026-07-31, up 36.54% from a year earlier.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The Communications Solutions Group supplied $1,345 million of that revenue, up 43%, and its operating income rose to $458 million from $246 million.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Wireline revenue passed wireless revenue for the first time in the company\u0027s history, which ties the growth to AI data centre spending.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:2},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Segment operating income reached $613 million against $338 million a year earlier, so the growth is reaching profit.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Management guided fourth-quarter revenue to $1.93 billion to $1.95 billion and non-GAAP earnings per share to $3.34 to $3.40 on about 172 million diluted shares.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Management also said demand is not the limiter and that its funnel is at an all-time high.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022At the next report the bull case needs revenue inside or above the $1.93 billion to $1.95 billion range and non-GAAP earnings per share of at least $3.34.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The bear case starts with supply, because management said supply chain will remain the governor of near-term revenue and that the supply environment is less flexible than a year ago.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The chief financial officer also said one-time tariff impacts artificially lifted fiscal 2026 profitability and will not repeat.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Costs are growing quickly, with research and development at $312 million, up 24.8%, and selling, general and administrative expense at $446 million, up 25.99%.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The growth is concentrated in the Communications Solutions Group, whose revenue is up 43% against 21.6% for the Electronic Industrial Solutions Group, so the result leans on AI infrastructure demand.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022At the next report the bear case needs revenue to fall short of the $1.93 billion low end of guidance, or earnings per share below $3.34, as supply limits how much demand converts to sales.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}]]}"
      }
